## Stack & Dev Commands

```
Stack: Tauri v2 + React 19 + Vite 7 + Bun/TS plugins + Tailwind CSS v4
Host:  ~317-line Rust lib.rs (Tokio async) + tauri-plugin-cors-fetch
IPC:   subprocess stdin/stdout JSON-RPC (bare JSON, no jsonrpc field)
UI:    Web Components (React compiled to IIFE via Vite)
Video: movi-player npm lib (WebCodecs + FFmpeg WASM), patched via bun patchedDependencies
```

```bash
bun run dev              # tauri dev (beforeDevCommand builds plugins + starts vite on 1420)
bun run build            # build:plugins + tauri build
bun run build:plugins    # build frontend WCs only
bun run dev:watch        # build:plugins --watch (background) + tauri dev
bun run tauri            # raw tauri CLI

# Standalone plugin testing (stdin JSON-RPC, one line per request)
echo '{"id":1,"method":"feed","params":{}}' | bun plugins/youtube/plugins/yt-feed/main.ts
echo '{"id":1,"method":"status","params":{}}' | bun plugins/youtube/plugins/yt-auth/main.ts
echo '{"id":1,"method":"list","params":{}}' | bun plugins/peertube/main.ts
```

- `tauri.conf.json`: `beforeDevCommand` = `bun run build:plugins && bunx vite --port 1420`, `devUrl` = `http://localhost:1420`, `withGlobalTauri: true`, `csp: null`
- Plugin backends import shared boilerplate via the bun path alias `#shared/*` → `./plugins/_shared/*` (declared in `package.json` `imports`)
- `movi-player@0.3.5` is patched via `patchedDependencies` + `patches/movi-player@0.3.5.patch` (tabindex/touchstart fix)

## Tauri Commands (3 total, in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`)

| Command | Signature | Purpose |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| `plugin_request` | `(method: "name.action", params: Value)` | Route RPC to plugin subprocess |
| `resolve_hook` | `(hook: "feed.video")` | Find which plugin provides a hook |
| `call_hook` | `(hook, method?, params?)` | Resolve hook + call it in one step |

All return `Result<Value, String>` — **rejects with plain strings**, not Error objects. In frontend code, use `??` not `||`:
```typescript
const msg = result.reason?.message ?? result.reason ?? "Unknown error"
```

15s `tokio::time::timeout` per request in the Rust host.

Rust host also registers two Tauri plugins (`lib.rs:276-277`): `tauri-plugin-opener` and `tauri-plugin-cors-fetch` (the CORS bypass — see Video Playback Pipeline below). The capability file `src-tauri/capabilities/default.json` grants `cors-fetch:default` alongside `core:default` + `opener:default`.

## Plugin Protocol

### Wire Format

Request: `{"id": <number>, "method": "<action>", "params": {}}` — newline-delimited JSON
Response: `{"id": <same>, "result": <any>}` or `{"id": <same>, "error": "<message>"}`

No `jsonrpc` field. Host prepends plugin name for routing (splits `"name.action"` on first `.`).

### Manifest Fields

| Field | Required | Description |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| `name` | ✅ | Unique plugin ID for RPC routing |
| `run` | ❌ | Spawn command, e.g. `"bun ./main.ts"` — `./` resolved relative to plugin dir |
| `methods` | ❌ | Array of method names, e.g. `["feed","resolve"]` |
| `hooks` | ❌ | Hook strings for capability resolution, e.g. `["feed.video","yt.auth"]` |
| `ui` | ❌ | WC tag for main UI — loaded AND mounted by App.tsx |
| `components` | ❌ | WC tags to build but NOT auto-mount, e.g. `["flux-player"]` |
| `slots` | ❌ | Named placeholders this plugin fills, e.g. `["video.player"]` |
| `feeds` | ❌ | Feed contributions: `[{type?, method?, card?}]` (`type` is legacy, slated for removal — see `.scratch/cleanup-legacy-fields/`) |

Plugin types:
- **Backend-only:** `run` present, no `ui`/`feeds`
- **Frontend-only (ui):** `ui` present, no `run` — loaded + mounted by App.tsx
- **Frontend-only (component):** `components` present, no `run` — built + loaded but NOT auto-mounted; created by slot consumers
- **Fullstack:** `run` + `ui`/`feeds`
- **Metadata:** neither `run` nor frontend fields — groups sub-plugins (e.g. `youtube`)

### Current Manifests (11 active; 7 spawned processes)

| Plugin | Type | Run | Notes |
|--------|------|-----|-------|
| core-manifest | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Recursive scan `plugins/**/plugin.json` |
| core-static | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Read files from `build/plugins/` (path whitelist enforced) |
| core-serve | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Vestigial — Vite handles serving |
| feed | Frontend (ui) | — | feed-widget WC (5-state machine) |
| youtube | Metadata | — | Parent container, no run/no ui |
| yt-feed | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Innertube home feed + stream resolve. hooks: `["feed.video"]`, methods: `["feed","resolve"]` |
| yt-auth | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Cookie auth from browser DBs. hooks: `["yt.auth"]`, methods: `["login","logout","status"]` |
| yt-search | Backend | `bun ./main.ts` | Innertube search. hooks: `["search"]`, methods: `["search"]` |
| peertube | Fullstack | `bun ./main.ts` | PeerTube API feed + card WC. hooks: `["feed.video"]`, methods: `["list","resolve"]` |
| player-modal | Frontend (ui) | — | Modal overlay shell. hooks: `["video.modal"]`. Resolves player slot at runtime |
| movi-player | Frontend (component) | — | Dir `plugins/flux-player/`, manifest name `movi-player`, tag `flux-player`. Wraps the movi-player npm lib. hooks: `["video.player"]`, components: `["flux-player"]`, slots: `["video.player"]` |

### Plugin `run` Field Resolution (`resolve_run` in `lib.rs:86`)
- Format: `"bun ./main.ts"` — first word = command, rest = args
- `./` or `../` args: joined with plugin dir (where `plugin.json` lives)
- Bare commands (bun, python3): passed through
- `current_dir` = plugin dir, env `PLUGIN_BASE_DIR` = project root
- Shared stdin/stdout boilerplate: `#shared/stdin.ts` — **processes requests serially** (an internal queue + busy flag; one request at a time per plugin process)

## Frontend Architecture

### Global Bridge API (declared in `App.tsx:6-18`)

```typescript
window.__pluginRpc(method, params)   // → invoke("plugin_request", {method, params})
window.resolveHook(hook)             // → invoke("resolve_hook", {hook})
window.callHook(hook, method, params) // → invoke("call_hook", {hook, method, params})
```

These are set before any WC scripts load. WC wrappers generated by the build script use custom element property setters (`_item`, `_manifests`) to receive data from React.

### App.tsx `init()` Flow (lines 33-82)
1. Call `core-manifest.scan` → get all manifests. On failure: red error `<p>` in `#feed-container`
2. Load WC scripts in order: `feeds[*].card` → `ui` → `components[]` (dedup via `loaded` Set; each loaded via `core-static.read` → `<script>` tag)
3. `uiPlugins[]` module-level array accumulates every manifest with a `ui` field (supports multiple mounted UIs)
4. Mount: clear `#feed-container`, then for each ui plugin `customElements.whenDefined(tag)` → `createElement` → set `.manifests = all` → append
5. `components[]` are loaded but **never** mounted by App.tsx — slot consumers (player-modal) create them imperatively

### Cross-Component Communication (CustomEvent Bridge)
- **Cards** dispatch `CustomEvent("video.player.load")` with `{url, title, source}` — `source = item._plugin` (the feed-source plugin name, injected by CardRenderer)
- **flux-player** (player) listens for `"video.player.load"` / `"video.player.hide"`. On load it calls `__pluginRpc(source + ".resolve", { url })` to get a playable stream URL, then creates a **fresh** `<movi-player>` element (never reuses the previous one — see Known Issues #3), sets `src`/`autoplay`, appends to its container, then dispatches `"video.modal.show"`. On resolve failure: logs and does NOT show the modal
- **player-modal** (modal) listens for `"video.modal.show"` / `"video.modal.hide"`; its Close button dispatches `"video.player.hide"`
- **feed-widget** listens for `video.modal.show` / `video.modal.hide` to hide/show itself
- Uses `window` as the event target (works across script bundles)
- Event names follow the hook-method convention `"<hook>.<method>"` — see CONTEXT.md

### Feed-Widget State Machine (`feed-widget.tsx`)
5 states: **systemError** → **loading** → **empty** → **partial** (items + yellow error banners) → **loaded**

Data flow:
1. Filter manifests to those with `feeds[]`
2. `Promise.allSettled` with per-source 15s timeout + 20s safety timer
3. Fisher-Yates shuffle items
4. CardRenderer creates card WCs imperatively: `document.createElement(tag)`, sets `data._plugin = plugin.name` (so the card knows which plugin resolves its URLs), then `card.item = rawItem`
5. Error banners search ALL manifests for plugin with `"login"` in methods (currently yt-auth), offer a "Sign in" button

### Video Playback Pipeline
- **resolve methods:** feed plugins expose a `resolve` RPC method that turns a feed/watch URL into a playable stream URL:
  - `yt-feed.resolve`: `tube.getStreamingData(videoId, { type: 'video+audio', format: 'mp4', quality: 'best' })` → `{ url }`
  - `peertube.resolve`: GET `/api/v1/videos/{uuid}` → `files[0].fileUrl` or `streamingPlaylists[0].playlistUrl` → `{ url }`
- **movi-player npm lib** (v0.3.5, patched): WebCodecs + FFmpeg WASM video engine, exposes the `<movi-player>` custom element; fetches bytes via `fetch()` through its HttpSource
- **tauri-plugin-cors-fetch** (v5): monkey-patches the global `fetch()` to route all HTTP through Rust reqwest (no CORS restrictions). Needed because PeerTube CDNs send no CORS headers; YouTube's CDN does. Zero plugin code changes. Caveat: every video byte chunk crosses Tauri IPC (`fetch_read_body`) — ~10-20 IPC calls/sec on HD; may stutter. See `.scratch/cors-proxy/spec.md`
- **player-modal slot resolution:** finds the provider via `manifests.find(m => m.slots?.includes("video.player"))`, reads `components[0]` for the tag, creates the WC once (guard ref), appends to its slot container

### Cookie Auth Flow
- **yt-auth** discovers browser cookies (Firefox/Chrome SQLite DBs) → writes `.youtube-cookie` file. Hook: `yt.auth`
- **yt-feed** reads `.youtube-cookie` at request time (lazy reload per request)
- Cookie file at `plugins/youtube/.youtube-cookie` (gitignored)
- 8s per-request timeout on `tube.getHomeFeed()` (JS-side `Promise.race`)
- Startup validation has empty `catch {}` (no destructive deletion on validation failure)
- `yt-feed` needs the Bun JS-evaluator shim: `Platform.shim.eval = (data) => new Function(data.output)()` (Bun has no `vm` module; required for decipher/nsig functions)

## Build Pipeline

### `bun run build:plugins` — `scripts/build-plugins.ts`
1. Recursive scan for `plugin.json` → collect tags from `ui`, `components[]`, `feeds[*].card` (dedup)
2. Per unique tag: find source in plugin dir (tsx > jsx > vue > svelte)
3. Auto-detect framework by scanning imports for `"react-dom"` vs `"preact"` vs `"vue"`
4. Generate temp `.vite.config.mjs` + `entry.tsx` (WC wrapper class: `_item`/`_manifests` setters, `createRoot`, error catch) + `style.css` (with `@import "tailwindcss"`)
5. `bunx vite build --config <config>` with `vite-plugin-css-injected-by-js` + `@tailwindcss/vite` → IIFE output to `build/plugins/<tag>.js`
6. Cleanup temp files
7. `--watch` mode: spawns per-tag `vite build --watch` processes; SIGINT kills watchers and cleans temp files

### Output (`build/plugins/`)
```
feed-widget.js     # ~160KB (React 19 IIFE)
yt-video-card.js   # ~156KB
peertube-card.js   # ~156KB
player-modal.js    # ~155KB
flux-player.js     # ~??KB (wraps movi-player lib)
```

### Quirks
- `needsRebuild`: checks mtime — delete `build/plugins/` for clean rebuild
- Cross-directory source: if source not in declaring plugin's dir, skip
- Temp files (`.vite.config.mjs`, `entry.tsx`, `style.css`) cleaned up after build; may remain if interrupted

## Known Issues (verify before trusting)

1. **LSP errors on `__pluginRpc`:** Not declared on `Window` type. Work at runtime (Tauri bridge sets them before WC scripts run). Cosmetic.
2. **`yt-auth` hook is `"yt.auth"`** in `plugin.json` — older docs/examples still say `"yt-auth"`. The rename is tracked in `.scratch/cleanup-legacy-fields/`.
3. **movi-player corrupts on failed load:** if a video fails to load (e.g. bad URL), the `<movi-player>` element's internal state is poisoned — reusing it makes subsequent videos fail with "Access denied" even with valid URLs. flux-player.tsx already works around this by creating a fresh element per load. Do not "optimize" that away.
4. **YouTube may still 403 on CDN even after resolve:** watch-page URLs are HTML, not streams — `yt-feed.resolve` must never fall back to the watch URL. If the resolved stream 403s, it's PoToken/SABR attestation territory — separate investigation (see `.scratch/cors-proxy/`).
5. **core-serve is vestigial:** spawned but unused; Vite dev server serves the frontend.

## Platform / Config Quirks

- **Window:** `decorations: false, transparent: true` — no chrome. All UI from Web Components.
- **No StrictMode:** Removed from `main.tsx` because React double-mount caused duplicate WC elements + redundant RPC calls.
- **Tailwind v4:** Uses `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin and `@import "tailwindcss"` syntax (not v3 config file approach).
- **Filesystem:** `/mnt/5TB/` is NTFS — Cargo builds are slow. Workaround: `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/flux-target` (set per-shell; no `.cargo/config.toml` in repo).
- **Memory:** 15GB RAM, ~11GB swap — constrained. Rust compilation is memory-intensive.
- **`plugins-disabled/`:** Contains old `video-player/`, `mpv-player/`, `yt-card/` plugins — moved out, not active.
- **`sessions/`:** Historical OpenCode session transcripts (`session-ses_*.md`). Not authoritative — use for debugging context only. Root-level copies are duplicates.
- **Issue tracker:** `.scratch/<feature>/` — active specs: `cors-proxy` (done), `player-feature` (ready-for-human), `cleanup-legacy-fields` (needs-info), `design-token-system` (ready-for-agent), `plugin-registry-system` (ready-for-agent).
- **opencode.json:** edit permissions deny all code files; only `.md`, `.scratch/**`, `lessons/*.html`, `assets/*`, `reference/*.html` are editable. `git *` requires ask.
- **Git:** working tree frequently has uncommitted changes (`git status` before assuming a file state).
